From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Tue, 19 Aug 2026 03:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: add SM6375 support

SM6375 uses the same ISP generation as QCM2290, which this driver already
supports: both describe csid530 and tfe530 in the vendor tree, so
csid_ops_340 and vfe_ops_340 apply unchanged. The CSIPHY is v1.2.1 rather
than v2.0.1 but is still a 3-phase PHY, so csiphy_ops_3ph_1_0 is reused.

Relative to QCM2290 this SoC has four CSIPHYs instead of two and three
CSID/TFE pairs instead of two. Register offsets, interrupts and clock
names come from blair-camera.dtsi in the Motorola SM6375 vendor tree
(rhodep's base DT is blair-moto-rhodep-base.dts); where the two SoCs
overlap the values are identical, including the CSID interrupts (210,
212), the CSIPHY interrupts (72, 73) and the TFE interrupts (211, 213).

Note the CSIPHY register windows are 0x2000 apart on this SoC rather than
QCM2290's 0x1000, which matches the different PHY revision.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
